joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4210bca39303e9a119439825e9b4456b9d2ce74b0b5d4ffc1fca97775d795734","event_uuid":"290c74c7-d48d-4e8d-a44a-a04e565e8822","position":{"commit_sha":"d22b17ae4e3dcbe824e7ca17e40cab2409824a03","position":"1787082779096963001-290c74c7-d48d-4e8d-a44a-a04e565e8822"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bd8725425b17bd2533619ea9fe1b1c7b15c988d51b052c3a087431b24d68de14","event_uuid":"373dae9e-3e7f-454b-addb-f3dc26acd8b0","position":{"commit_sha":"59d8c6829f6c5955e8bfbef1f1b4097225acbaca","position":"1787082794436565001-373dae9e-3e7f-454b-addb-f3dc26acd8b0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ece22da4f1561906496d611d336225288ec880eeef4b4432137121fc973a9699","event_uuid":"0753eeda-d082-433d-919d-eaf1b7d5856c","position":{"commit_sha":"b2e0a8364e0ec4f32fa6024d8bb8f4d34138e96c","position":"1787083082070955001-0753eeda-d082-433d-919d-eaf1b7d5856c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3303a3ea0f3118f4e5cf599955468d1937f852dce087c26bdfdd892ee35dfd4b","event_uuid":"4d4b8602-41cb-449c-97b8-180547dc7ba9","position":{"commit_sha":"8dd7cf5f69f8e8597325699ecb03e36755dbb43c","position":"1787084070767416001-4d4b8602-41cb-449c-97b8-180547dc7ba9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 confirmed root cause and legitimacy. Dynamic proof: in an ephemeral git-backed tracker, I created an in-progress bug, minted a cryptographically certified completion-verifier PASS whose verified-at-sha equaled the close ref, verified that stored record as certified, replaced the completion provider with a counting spy, and closed at that exact SHA. Current main called the provider once. The probe passed only when asserting calls == 1, then the temporary instrumentation was removed and the worktree returned clean.\n\nMechanism: close_precheck._completion_precheck (src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:639-652) unconditionally calls close_autoresume.verify_with_auto_resume after deterministic guards. That helper enters its loop and calls llm.verify_completion immediately (src/rebar/_commands/close_autoresume.py:91-138); it never reads the existing completion-verifier attestation. The signature path already authenticates the record and exposes its signed SHA/material fields (src/rebar/signing.py:656-680; src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py:463-505), and current_material_fingerprint supplies the freshness comparison. The closed adolescent-evilminded-locust ticket is not a duplicate: it retries insufficiency-only FAILs within one close and deliberately invokes the provider again.\n\nThe user-approved ticket contract establishes defect legitimacy: a valid ticket-contained attested PASS at the same resolved ref must be reused, while invalid/stale/different-ref evidence must fall through to fresh verification. The standalone verify-completion command is render-only and produced no stored attestation in the motivating sequence; changing it into a mutating producer is explicitly out of scope. Expected post-fix behavior: an eligible same-ref stored completion op-cert yields zero provider calls, then the existing locked close and post-close signing path runs unchanged. Caller sweep: verify_with_auto_resume has one production caller, the shared close precheck used by CLI/MCP/library closes; no caller depends on paying for a redundant verifier run. All ineligible records retain the current provider path.","timestamp":1787082794436565001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 2 local verification complete. Held-out lifecycle oracle: current main was RED because the real CLI close called the provider once despite a certified same-ref completion op-cert; after the held-out fixer added the reuse eligibility check, all 9 cases are GREEN. Deleting the reuse dispatch restored the exact RED (one provider call), then restoring it returned GREEN. Negative controls prove fresh verification for changed ref, FAIL, wrong kind, missing SHA, missing material, material drift, post-reopen staleness, and unverifiable signature. Existing completion auto-resume, explicit-ref signing, attested-signing, and signature suites remain green: 64 focused tests passed. make lint, make typecheck, complexity ratchet, module-size check (close_autoresume.py 279 LOC), and diff check pass. Parity census: CLI transition, public library transition, and MCP transition_ticket all converge on transition_close.close_ticket -> _completion_precheck -> the shared reuse seam; automated dual-direction surface is N/A. No new dependency, no test weakening, and standalone verify-completion remains render-only/out of scope. Change is locally ready to commit and will wait behind active Gerrit change 1867.","timestamp":1787084070767416001}],"created_at":1787081945007848001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6bdd7f83-dc3b-4504-99f8-49ac2f6c4aa6","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5bc2-2a95-6744-4d14"}],"description":"## Context\nA completion close always dispatches the billable verifier after deterministic guards, even when the ticket already carries a cryptographically certified `completion-verifier` PASS bound to the exact immutable commit being closed. The existing signature verifier can authenticate the stored completion op-cert, but the close seam never consults it. A runtime probe created a certified same-ref completion record on an in-progress bug, then closed at that exact SHA: the provider spy was called once.\n\nThe earlier standalone `verify-completion` command returns a signable result but does not persist an attestation. Changing that command into a mutating producer is out of scope; reuse applies only when a genuine ticket-contained completion attestation already exists (for example, from the trusted op-cert producer). The closed Locust task concerns bounded retry of insufficiency-only FAILs and is not a duplicate.\n\n## Proven root cause\n`src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py::_completion_precheck` unconditionally calls `close_autoresume.verify_with_auto_resume` after its deterministic guards. `verify_with_auto_resume` immediately invokes `llm.verify_completion`; neither seam checks the ticket's existing `completion-verifier` attestation. The required verifier, SHA pin, and material fingerprint are already available from the signature and plan-material infrastructure.\n\n## Repair plan\n- Add a fail-safe reuse check at the close auto-resume seam before provider dispatch.\n- Resolve the close target ref once and require the stored completion op-cert to certify cryptographically.\n- Require an authenticated `completion-verifier: PASS` manifest.\n- Require the authenticated `verified-at-sha` to equal the resolved close target SHA.\n- Require the authenticated material fingerprint to equal the ticket's current material fingerprint.\n- Reject attestations invalidated by a later reopen.\n- Return a close-compatible reused PASS result so the normal close, durable verdict, and post-close signing path remain unchanged.\n- Fall through to the existing verifier for every absent, malformed, unverifiable, stale, differently pinned, or otherwise ineligible record.\n\n## Test contract card\n- authoritative_contract: operator-approved same-ref attested-PASS reuse requirement on this ticket.\n- trigger_preconditions: ticket is in progress; completion gate enabled; a completion-verifier op-cert is already stored; explicit --ref resolves to the op-cert SHA.\n- production_path: transition -> close precheck -> close autoresume/reuse seam -> locked close -> completion signing.\n- observable_postcondition: provider call count is zero and the ticket closes signed.\n- negative_controls: different SHA, invalid signature, missing pin, stale material, and pre-reopen attestation each call the provider exactly once.\n- test_tier: lifecycle integration over an ephemeral git repo and real ticket store, with only the provider replaced by a spy.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A close at the exact SHA of a valid stored completion PASS makes zero completion-provider calls.\n- [ ] A reused PASS still produces a signed closed ticket.\n- [ ] A reused PASS leaves durable completion evidence for the closed ticket.\n- [ ] A changed resolved ref forces a fresh completion verification.\n- [ ] A cryptographically invalid completion record forces a fresh completion verification.\n- [ ] A non-PASS or wrong-kind record forces a fresh completion verification.\n- [ ] An attestation without an authenticated SHA pin forces a fresh completion verification.\n- [ ] An attestation without an authenticated material fingerprint forces a fresh completion verification.\n- [ ] A material fingerprint mismatch forces a fresh completion verification.\n- [ ] An attestation invalidated by a later reopen forces a fresh completion verification.\n- [ ] Explicit CLI `--ref` reaches the reuse decision through the normal lifecycle path.\n- [ ] Focused tests pass.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` passes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_autoresume.py","reason":"validate and reuse eligible same-ref completion attestations before provider dispatch"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_attestation_reuse.py","reason":"held-out lifecycle RED/GREEN and fail-safe negative controls"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"32e893ce-047e-41d6-b77f-cec0a448cea7","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["completion-verifier","performance","gates"],"ticket_id":"e671-56bf-4022-46b5","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reuse same-ref attested completion verification during close","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["454a5f19-3183-4091-b73f-fe0d372911f3","6bdd7f83-dc3b-4504-99f8-49ac2f6c4aa6","fe86127c-f540-445b-a17d-e559eac0c3cd","32e893ce-047e-41d6-b77f-cec0a448cea7","900eb888-cba1-448d-ab93-70c81eaa311f","9bafcd64-d1c6-449d-a60b-125e6821f925","290c74c7-d48d-4e8d-a44a-a04e565e8822","373dae9e-3e7f-454b-addb-f3dc26acd8b0","0753eeda-d082-433d-919d-eaf1b7d5856c","4d4b8602-41cb-449c-97b8-180547dc7ba9"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787089249820650001,"uuid":"c38b099b-3a7b-42fc-a4db-0cbabc7deb5a"}